        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrew Dudley\n- Places: Broughty Castle, Broughty Ferry, Dundee, Scotland, River Tay\n- Events: War of the Rough Wooing\n- Roles: Admiral of the fleet, commander of the English garrison\n\nFacts:\n- In 1547–1548, Andrew Dudley acted as admiral of the fleet.\n- In 1547–1548, Andrew Dudley participated in the War of the Rough Wooing in Scotland.\n- During the War of the Rough Wooing, Andrew Dudley commanded the English garrison of Broughty Castle.\n- Broughty Castle is a historic castle on the banks of the River Tay in Broughty Ferry, Dundee, Scotland.",
